WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.124 --> 00:00:05.252
(Tywin): Rhaegar Targaryen
lay dead on the banks of the Trident,

00:00:05.253 --> 00:00:09.173
his royal army shattered and in retreat.

00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:13.886
The days of the dragon kings
were clearly numbered.

00:00:13.887 --> 00:00:17.556
Until that moment, it would have been 
foolish to commit Casterly Rock

00:00:17.557 --> 00:00:21.643
to either the Crown or the rebellion.

00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:26.106
What would our family have to gain
in supporting a raving madman?

00:00:26.107 --> 00:00:31.107
Or in entering a crusade to put
Robert Baratheon on the Iron Throne?

00:00:31.362 --> 00:00:34.490
But chaos benefits no one.

00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:37.367
It was time for House Lannister
to do what it could

00:00:37.368 --> 00:00:42.122
to ensure a return of peace and prosperity
to the land.

00:00:42.123 --> 00:00:45.959
I, Tywin Lannister,
brought 10,000 Lannister troops

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.961
to the gates of King's Landing,

00:00:47.962 --> 00:00:52.962
in order to bring the bloodshed
to a quick and decisive conclusion.

00:00:53.009 --> 00:00:56.011
King Aerys had been
sending ravens for months,

00:00:56.012 --> 00:00:59.515
begging for my support to end the uprising.

00:00:59.516 --> 00:01:03.185
In a way, his pleas had been answered.

00:01:03.186 --> 00:01:08.186
As I had suspected, Aerys opened
the city gates and welcomed my men.

00:01:10.193 --> 00:01:11.777
Our plan was clear -

00:01:11.778 --> 00:01:14.363
crush Aerys' remaining bannermen

00:01:14.364 --> 00:01:16.949
and remove the remnants
of the royal family

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.911
as quickly and efficiently as possible.

00:01:20.912 --> 00:01:24.248
Any alternative meant years of further war

00:01:24.249 --> 00:01:28.043
and a fragmented Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:28.044 --> 00:01:30.420
Our means were bloody,

00:01:30.421 --> 00:01:34.341
but the results speak for themselves.

00:01:34.342 --> 00:01:39.342
As for Aerys, it is true
he met his fate at the hands of my son.

00:01:40.557 --> 00:01:43.350
Aerys had kept Jaime close
during the rebellion,

00:01:43.351 --> 00:01:47.396
thinking himself clever
in keeping my son as a hostage

00:01:47.397 --> 00:01:51.817
should I decide to pledge support
to the rebel cause.

00:01:51.818 --> 00:01:54.903
This proved to be his greatest mistake,

00:01:54.904 --> 00:01:59.904
for, when the time came,
Jaime did his duty as a Lannister...

00:02:00.743 --> 00:02:04.121
and drove his sword
into the Mad King's back.

00:02:04.122 --> 00:02:09.122
With that,
Robert Baratheon's crown was secured.

00:02:09.252 --> 00:02:13.714
The new king recognized our role
in his ascension to the throne,

00:02:13.715 --> 00:02:16.049
just as he recognized how useful

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.803
the might and riches
of Casterly Rock would be...

00:02:19.804 --> 00:02:22.931
if he wanted to keep it.

00:02:22.932 --> 00:02:27.932
To that end,
I offered my daughter Cersei as his queen.

00:02:28.021 --> 00:02:32.441
Had Aerys not spurned
this same offer years earlier...

00:02:32.442 --> 00:02:35.193
perhaps things would have
worked out differently.

00:02:35.194 --> 00:02:40.194
With Robert and Cersei crowned
as king and queen of the Seven Kingdoms,

00:02:40.241 --> 00:02:42.451
it was a new day.

00:02:42.452 --> 00:02:44.369
The dragon was vanquished

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:49.370
and the Seven Kingdoms
would thereafter belong to the Stag.

00:02:49.626 --> 00:02:54.626
And the Lion.

